		"_comment": "Conquest large WALL lantern position fix. Conquest's large/wall.json has the glass BODY and the WALLMOUNT bracket as two independent top-level groups, and the body sits mispositioned relative to the bracket. The fix (found by editing the shape in Blockbench): wrap both groups in a single parent 'overall' group so the body shares the bracket's coordinate frame, which seats it correctly (the small/wall lantern is authored this way and renders right). This patch reproduces that: it ADDs the 'overall' wrapper (our own values), MOVEs the existing 'lantern' and 'wallmount' nodes into it (relocating Conquest's nodes, not restating their geometry), and replaces the handful of transform scalars that come with the wrapping plus the glass-panel positions. COORDINATE/STRUCTURE ONLY: ships no Conquest textures or shape wholesale. dependsOn conquest gates it to the pack (also the shape's owner) and orders it after Conquest. NB: element/child indices mirror Conquest 1.0.7 large/wall.json (top-level [wallmount, lantern]; lantern children [...frames..., base, lid, candle, grid, glass]) - re-verify these paths if Conquest reorganises that shape (see docs/HANDOFF-conquest.md)."
